{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 9, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a member of the House of Toulouse and the Count of Tripoli from 1152 until his death in 1187. He was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. \n\nHe succeeded his father in 1152 and married Eschiva of Arsur in 1152. He had two children with her a son Bohemond and a daughter Melisende. *Family* \n\nRaymond III supported the military orders in the region particularly the Knights Hospitaller and the Knights Templar. He also supported the kingdom of Jerusalem. He participated in the Battle of Montgisard in 1177 and the Battle of Marj Ayyun in 1179. He also participated in the Battle of Hattin in 1187 which was a decisive defeat for the kingdom of Jerusalem.\n\nAfter the Battle of Hattin Raymond III fled to the castle of Raymond II's brother Bertrand of Tripoli in Tortosa. He later moved to the castle of Raymond III's ally Raymond III Count of Toulouse in Margat. However in 1187 he was forced to surrender to Saladin. He was imprisoned and died in 1187. *Prison and Death*\n\nRaymond III was a key figure in the region due to his strategic alliances and military campaigns. He played a significant role in the kingdom of Jerusalem's military campaigns and the growth of the military orders in the region. His strategic alliances with the military orders and the kingdom of Jerusalem helped to secure the region against external threats.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.014390614}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -0.00016938205}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -0.0010648064}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.1300828}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -3.349725e-05}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -0.00021371941}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -6.651657e-05}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.015882885}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.34376433}, {"token": " member", "logprob": -0.5870414}, {"token": " of", "logpr